 "text": "9/29/26, 10:19 AM\n\nDisconnection/Reconnection of a Utility Installation\n\nUse\n\nThis component enables you to manage disconnections and reconnections. This component is optional. You need to use it if you\n\nwant to temporarily interrupt supply to customers (especially within the bounds of a legal dunning procedure). A disconnection is\na temporary interruption in the supply of a utility service that does not involve the meter removal. This is due to the following\nreasons, for example:\n\ne Introduction of a collection procedure for outstanding payment\n\ne Technical disconnection due to request of utilities company or customer\n\nIn the first instance, the service is resumed (reconnection) when the customer has paid the outstanding bill; in the second, it is\ndone at the request of the customer.\n\nDisconnections and Reconnections in an Advanced Metering Infrastructure Environment\n\nIf you are working in an advanced metering infrastructure (AMI) environment, you can find more information under Advanced\nMetering Infrastructure.\n\nIntegration\nNotifying Customers of Upcoming Disconnections and Reconnections\n\nDepending on legal requirements or on intra-enterprise guidelines, y ou might be required to contact your customers before you\ncarry out a disconnection or reconnection. The customer contact process is called Notification. In such situations, you (or a CRM\nagent) need to execute additional steps between the disconnection or reconnection request and the actual disconnection or\nreconnection.\n\nInvoicing\n\nYou can invoice flat-rate charges for a disconnection or reconnection using the SAP Utilities component (IS-U). For more\n\ninformation, see the Invoicing component.\n\nIf you create a service order for the field service employee, and want to invoice the order then you require the Customer Service\n(CS) and Sales and Distribution (SD) components. For more information, see View: Customer Service (CS) and Plant Maintenance\n(PM) and Sales and Distribution.\n\nConfirming Disconnection and Reconnection Order Data\n\nYou can confirm disconnection and reconnection order data in the system using the IDoc ISU DISC UPLOAD (IS-U/CCS:\nupload disconnection/reconnection order data).\n\nFor more information about IDocs see the following documentation:\n\ne For general information, see IDoc Interface/Electronic Data Interchange\n\ne@ Enr datailad infarmatinn caa l]Ilcing Narit;mantatinn Tanic\n",
